====================================================================================================
§2  THE LANE [D1] AND ITS TIMING CLOSURE [D7] (in-model)
====================================================================================================
logic cells: select 1024 + sign 32 + weight fan-out 384 + 248 full adders x 15 = 5160; Wallace 236 FAs in 8 stages (87 pass-through bit-stages) + 12-bit ripple adder
depth model: 5472 wires, critical path 92 cells (~31 ps at ~0.33 ps/cell = 2.1 slots); largest wait of a wire for its last consumer: 44 cells; output bits span depths 26-92 (fixed per readout line, deskewed at the receiver)
balancing buffers to regenerate every waiting wire (latch-free wave pipeline): tolerance 0 cells -> 2,616 (+51%), tolerance 4 cells -> 581 (+11%), tolerance 14 cells -> 189 (+4%)
re-sync stations (one per wire crossing each cut): spacing 10.0 -> 679, spacing 13.3 -> 393 (the earlier cell-fraction rule gave 215-516)
   timing-closed lane, t0: 8,169-8,455 cells
   timing-closed lane, t4: 6,134-6,420 cells
   timing-closed lane, t14: 5,742-6,028 cells
reference lane (t = 0, as Part I's half adder balances its own paths with a DLY cell): 8,169-8,455 cells, 0.224-0.232 mm^2
lane power at 300 K (tau^-3 scaled, hydrodynamic tier): 64-86 mW -> 29-39 fJ/MAC at full utilisation
lane power at 353 K (kinetic-corrected, Part I 8.2): 130-141 mW -> 59-64 fJ/MAC at full utilisation

====================================================================================================
§3  TRY: GATE-LEVEL EMULATION ON BONSAI-SHAPED MATRICES [D1][D2]
====================================================================================================
the netlist's exactness is also provable: every full adder keeps s + 2c = a + b + c_in, and each product's 8-bit pattern (one's complement for w = -1, sign bit inverted) is an unsigned u in [0, 255], so the tree output U = sum(u) lies in [0, 8160] < 2^13; the emulation checks the implementation of that argument
ATT k (full matrix)             :   163,840 block sums (  5.2 M MACs) through the gate-level netlist in  0.3 s -> all exact: True; CMOS scaling code reproduces the int8 reference: True; vs unquantised float 45.4 dB (Q8_0 only)
GDN ssm_out (full matrix)       :   983,040 block sums ( 31.5 M MACs) through the gate-level netlist in  1.6 s -> all exact: True; CMOS scaling code reproduces the int8 reference: True; vs unquantised float 45.0 dB (Q8_0 only)
FFN down (1,024 of 5,120 rows)  :   557,056 block sums ( 17.8 M MACs) through the gate-level netlist in  2.2 s -> all exact: True; CMOS scaling code reproduces the int8 reference: True; vs unquantised float 45.6 dB (Q8_0 only)
(BER = 0: the threshold cells act as Boolean logic, so this is a netlist check, not a physics check)

