1.0 TB/s ->  176.4 tok/s -> 3 lanes (68% busy); 25,531-26,389 cells (0.70-0.72 mm^2); fabric 0.20-0.27 W (300 K), 0.41-0.44 W (353 K); 1.1-2.5 mJ/token
      launch 448 lines (30.9 Tb/s), readout 39 lines (2.69 Tb/s); 4.67 launched bits per MAC computed
3.0 TB/s ->  529.2 tok/s -> 7 lanes (88% busy); 60,255-62,257 cells (1.65-1.71 mm^2); fabric 0.47-0.64 W (300 K), 0.96-1.04 W (353 K); 0.9-2.0 mJ/token
      launch 704 lines (48.6 Tb/s), readout 91 lines (6.28 Tb/s); 3.14 launched bits per MAC computed
cooled to 77 K (Joule model [D3] extended below the hydrodynamic expiry, uncertified): cell power x0.125 -> 0.059-0.079 W for the 7 lanes; Carnot work at 77 K x2.90 -> wall-plug 0.23-0.31 W at ideal cooling (x0.49 the warm fabric power)
heat: fill 3.6% -> dT = 2.8-3.7 K at 0.78-1.02 kW/cm^2 (300 K) vs the 55 K budget
heat: fill 3.6% -> dT = 5.8-6.1 K at 1.59-1.67 kW/cm^2 (353 K kinetic) vs the 55 K budget
Part I's only system-scale figure is illustrative (8.1: 'a 1 W-class drive over 1e4-1e5 active cells'), not a cap
within 1e5 cells: 11 timing-closed lanes -> 949 tok/s with batching (B >= 2 at 3 TB/s)

CMOS perimeter per token: 2.40 GFLOP of block-sum scaling (1.27 TFLOP/s at 529 tok/s), n_neg popcounts 800 M (fixed by the weights: precompute and stream +10.6%, or count in CMOS), FWHT 21.7-29.1 M adds, GDN ~151 M FP32 MAC, attention 0.81 G MAC at 4k context
